    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228-a3">

                <pb facs="0664" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg450"/>

                <head>General Schenck to Earl
                        Granville</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">South Kensington Hotel</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Queen’s Gate Terrace,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 29, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Lord Granville:</hi> Many thanks for your
                    thoughtful attention in giving me information of the success of the United
                    States forces against the Coreans. I received your note last evening and
                    immediately telegraphed its contents to Mr. Fish; although I see by the morning
                    papers they received the same news yesterday at Washington.</p>
                <p>Sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROB’T C. SCHENCK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
